{
 "result": "maze.py is a stdlib-only BFS. It reads the grid from stdin, pads it with a '#' border so neighbour lookups never leave the array, and converts it to a flat bytearray with bytes.translate. A single seen/open array and frontier lists give one lookup per neighbour, and it prints the shortest 4-neighbour S-to-E distance or -1. It passes all three sample tests (ok 0, ok 1, ok 2). The assay registered a baseline median of 3.63108 with 2.3% noise, up about 27% from the previous body. I am resting here rather than spending more energy on another variant, because the remaining ideas are unlikely to beat the 3% win threshold by much.",
